Fixes (all in harness/model-guide/):

- preview.sh (F1, F2, F4): a bash scan refuses any symlink under docs/ with
  `preview: refused path <absolute link path>` on stdout, exit 2, empty
  stderr, before any write; the link target stays byte-identical. A second
  bash scan refuses an unreadable docs entry (mode 000) with
  `preview: unreadable <path relative to the repo>` on stdout, exit 2, empty
  stderr, before any write: no half-built preview folder stays, and an
  existing preview folder stays byte-identical. Both scans run before
  mkdir -p and cp. The Python heredoc lost the dead `sys.exit(2)` branch,
  which had no `import sys`; the scans cover the case. The A3-3 planted-link
  refusal line stays `preview: refused path <link path>` (F4).
- publish.ts (F2, F3): the docs walk stats each entry with lstatSync and
  never follows a link. A symlink (to a file or to a directory) and any
  non-regular entry land in the broken list; readdirSync is wrapped, so an
  unreadable directory maps to the same list. Each broken entry prints
  `publish: drift <path relative to docs/>`, exit 2, empty stderr, no write,
  no stack trace, and the copy loop never writes through a link. The drift
  output order stays sorted; the approval rows stay checked first.
- Headers: the preview.sh header names the `preview: refused path <absolute
  link path>` line for a docs symlink and the `preview: unreadable <path
  relative to the repo>` line for an unreadable entry. The publish.ts
  header names the `publish: drift <path>` line for a symlink or an
  unreadable directory and states that the walk never follows a link.

Brief vs tests: no difference. The tests are the source of truth for the
exact refusal texts and were followed.

